# The pages are hand-authored, and `interview-prep/check.js` reads them as raw
# bytes and fails on any CR — so line endings are load-bearing for them.
#
# With `core.autocrlf=true` (git's default on Windows) git rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout, which would both churn every diff and make the checker report
# CRLF on a file nobody touched. Declaring these `-text` pins them to LF in the
# working tree on every platform.
interview-prep/**/*.html    -text
interview-prep/**/*.css     -text

# The catalogue wall is checked by the same checker (`--index`) under the same
# rules, and it was NOT pinned before the two index pages were retired — so on a
# Windows checkout git would hand it CRLF and every `--index` run would fail on a
# file nobody touched.
index.html                  -text

# The self-hosted webfonts are binary. Without this, git's text detection would
# be free to rewrite them and quietly corrupt every face on the site.
fonts/*.woff2               -text binary